======================================================================
PART 1: TRANSFER MATRIX EIGENVALUES — THE HELIX
======================================================================

The S112 transfer matrix for NUD (No Unit Descent) counting is:
  M(x) = [[1, 2x, 0],
           [0,  0, 1],
           [1,  x, 0]]

Characteristic polynomial: λ³ - λ² - xλ - x = 0
Factored: (λ-1)(λ²) = x(λ+1), i.e., λ²(λ-1) = x(λ+1)

SPECIAL VALUES:
  x=0: λ³ - λ² = 0  →  eigenvalues {0, 0, 1}
  x=1: λ³ - λ² - λ - 1 = 0  →  TRIBONACCI equation!
  x=2: λ³ - λ² - 2λ - 2 = 0  →  OCF parameter (H = I(Ω,2))

Tribonacci constant τ₃ = 1.8392867552
Complex conjugate roots at x=1: -0.419643+0.606291j, -0.419643-0.606291j
  Modulus: |z| = 0.737353
  Argument: arg(z) = 2.176234 rad = 124.69°

Golden ratio φ = 1.6180339887
Ratio τ₃/φ = 1.136742

--- OPEN-Q-029 Verification ---
τ₃^8 = 130.977154
131 (numerator of Var/Mean² at n=7)
Difference: τ₃^8 - 131 = -0.022846
Fractional part of log_τ₃(131) = 0.000286

Tribonacci numbers: [1, 1, 2, 4, 7, 13, 24, 44, 81, 149, 274, 504, 927, 1705, 3136]
T(12) = 927  (OPEN-Q-029 says denominator 504)
T(13) = 1705  ← this is 504!
So 131/504 ≈ τ₃^8 / T(13)
  τ₃^8 / T(13) = 0.076819
  131 / 504 = 0.259921

